A||||2||RedRavenGT||Little white bubbles???||||1||
Z||000000||RedRavenGT||09-17-2001||09:10 PM||||Well, lately my car has been running pretty crappy. Looked under the car and I know I do have an oil leak. I have recently put on a new oil pan gasket so I know that isnt the culprit. However I did see some oil on the top of the tranny up near the front heads. ( I didnt really look that hard to see where it was coming from. Also I checked the oil and there are some little white bubbles in the oil? <P>Any idea? <BR>Head gasket?<P>TIA<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>(formerly known as V8Fiero)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redraven.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LS1swap||09-17-2001||09:47 PM||||It might be leaking from the distributor base both mine and a friend of mines did leaked there. I think it was an O-ring seal. My friend just fixed his I will ask him and make another reply tomorrow. It has been about four years since I did mine so it is hard to remember. But I know it fixed the problem. Ps you will need to index both the rotor and the distributor base to make sure you put it back in the correct position.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Areakon||09-18-2001||01:00 AM||||The little white bubbles could be coolent. Can you smell any antifreeze in the exhaust? Is it running any hotter then normal? Is it building excessive pressure in the coolent system? If you run it with the coolent cap off can you see any bubbles in the coolent?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
